==English==
[[Image:Valeriana officinalis jfg1.jpg|thumb|A '''valerian''' plant in bloom.]]
{{wikipedia|valerian (plant)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|valeriane|lang=fro}} or mediaeval {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|valeriana|lang=la}}, from the personal name {{term|Valerius}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/vəˈlɪəɹɪən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hardy]] [[perennial]] [[flowering plant]], {{taxlink|Valeriana officinalis|species}}, with heads of [[sweet]]ly [[scent]]ed pink or white [[flower]]s.
# More generally, any plant of the genus ''[[Valeriana]]''.
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The root of ''Valeriana officinalis'', used in herbal medicine.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Valeriana officinalis}} [[allheal]], [[cat thyme]]

